{"files":[{"file":"<fixture>","diagnostics":[{"code":"P-DO-ENDS-IN-BINDING","help":"end the block with the expression whose value it should have, such as `pure x` or the call that produces the result; a binding (`let` or `x <- e`) only names a value for the statements after it","kind":"parse","message":"a `do` block must end in an expression, but its last statement is a binding (`let` or `<-`) — a `do` block's value is its last expression","range":{"end":{"character":3,"line":10},"start":{"character":2,"line":10}},"severity":1,"source":"medaka"}]}]}
